# Vendored and generated trees, ignored so a whole-tree run
# (`prettier --write .`) behaves the same in every boltmesh repo. The
# pre-commit hooks are file-scoped and would not reach most of these
# anyway; this matters for the ad-hoc whole-tree runs.
#
# The first block is identical across the repos; anything below it is
# specific to this one.
# Scope note: in this repo markdown is markdownlint's job, not prettier's, so
# a bare `prettier --write .` will still want to rewrap the .md files. Use the
# pre-commit hook (or the npm script where one exists) rather than a whole-tree
# write.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/

# client-specific generated trees
/.dart_tool/
/.flutter-plugins
/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
/.pub-cache/
/.idea/
/.vscode/
/android/.gradle/
/ios/Pods/
/macos/Pods/

# Xcode owns these; the pre-commit hook excludes them too, but a whole-tree
# run reaches them without going through the hook.
ios/Runner/Assets.xcassets/
macos/Runner/Assets.xcassets/
